N2  - Quantum Convolutional Neural Network (QCNN) is an integration of classical convolutional neural networks and quantum computing, designed to leverage the unique advantages of quantum computing to enhance machine learning models. It holds promise for providing novel perspectives in solving complex pattern recognition tasks. In the process of image recognition, factors such as the type of convolutional layers, pooling layers, and sample sets significantly influence the recognition results. This study conducts experimental validation on QCNN-based image recognition, investigating the impact of different convolutional layer types, pooling layer types, and image sample datasets on the accuracy of QCNN recognition. Additionally, future development trends of QCNN are discussed.


