N2  - Dynamic DNA nanotechnology enables applications in biosensing, molecular computing, and nanorobotics. Toeholdmediated strand displacement (TMSD) is a key mechanism in these systems. In this study, we replace a classical convolutional neural network (CNN) with a quantum convolutional neural network (QCNN), leveraging TensorFlow Quantum (TFQ) to predict TMSD rate constants ($\boldsymbol{k}_{\mathbf{1}}$). Using a dataset of $\mathbf{4 4 5 0}$ DNA sequences with simulated $\boldsymbol{k}_{\mathbf{1}}$ values, we combine DNA-BERT embeddings with nucleotide availability and GC affinity features. The proposed QCNN model demonstrates strong performance, achieving an RMSE of 0.79 and $\mathbf{R}^{\mathbf{2}}$ of 0.74, comparable to the classical CNN. This demonstrates the promise of hybrid quantumclassical machine learning in the field of DNA nanotechnology.


