N2  - As the use of AI-generated text increases, so does the need to identify such content and prevent such inappropriative intents such as misinformation, plagiarism, and unauthorized content generation. The Deep Fast Quantum Convolutional Neural Network (DF-QCNN) has become a promising model for such a use as quantum computing can help improve feature extraction and classification. But for the DF-QCNN, it is somewhat complex in the sense that the weight parameters optimization has to be done on a high dimension, non-concave space. Previous optimization approaches including first and second order gradient descent techniques often take long time for convergence, are sensitive to local minimum and thus provide low accuracy. To overcome these limitations, it is proposed to use a novel metaheuristic algorithm called the Crayfish Optimization Algorithm (CFO) based on the movement behavior of crayfish in a complex environment. CFO is well structured to exercise both exploration and exploitation and maintain efficient optimization of weight parameters. The integration of CFO with the proposed DF-QCNN enhances text detection accuracy, shortens convergence time as well as increases computational efficiency than by using of traditional approaches of optimization.


