N2  - With the advancement of technology, the need for better computation is increasing. Quantum computers uses quantum bit or qubit as the smallest computational unit. Each qubit has the capabilities of storing the value of 0 and 1 at the same time. The number of qubit needed to do computation is increased logarithmically instead of increasing proportionally like in classical bits. Quantum Convolutional Neural Network (QCNN) is an algorithm developed based on CNN that allows quantum computer to do what classical computer can do using CNN. However, QCNN is a relatively new technology and thus have rooms for improvement. The purpose of this research is to develop an algoritm using quantum computing technology to finish a task with less computational resources compared to only using classical algorithm with good enough accuracy. The task that will be done by the system is detecting the position of a line in a 2 × 4 pixel image. The result is the accuracy from the quantum hybrid algorithm is 93,7%, which is less than classical algorithm at 100%. But the number of parameter needed for hybrid algorithm is only 1,354 parameters instead of 10,058 parameters used by classical algorithm.


