N2  - Mobile Ad Hoc Networks (MANETs) are spontaneous, self-configuring wireless networks employed in life-critical environments such as disaster relief and battlefield applications. Their infrastructure-less topology renders them extremely sensitive to threats such as eavesdropping, routing attacks, and application-level attacks, resulting in high latency, low network throughput, and diminished network lifetime. Conventional security measures are incapable of effectively responding to dynamic network dynamics, resulting in the necessity for a sophisticated blockchain-based security system. The proposed method, Blockchain-based Stereoscopic Scalable Quantum Convolutional Neural Network with Swarm Bipolar Algorithm (SSQCNNet-SBA), increases security in blockchain of MANET while maintaining Quality of Service (QoS) and network integrity management. It starts with node authentication through an Efficient Quantum Blockchain with QDPoS, where only authenticated nodes are involved in routing. The Stereoscopic Scalable Quantum Convolutional Neural Network (SSQCNNet) analyzes and optimizes the routes, and the Swarm Bipolar Algorithm (SBA) refines them due to topology changes in the network. The proposed method has an achieved throughput of 55.8 Mbps, delay of 72 ms, packet delivery ratio of 97.2%, and energy consumption of 6.1 J, while preserving a network lifetime of 97.5% for 100 nodes. This approach delivers secure, adaptive, and resilient MANET routing, significantly improving network security, performance, and lifespan in highly dynamic environments.


