N2  - A key challenge in color image classification is the efficient representation of Red, Green and Blue channels while preserving the inherent inter channel relationships. Traditional Convolutional Neural Networks(CNNs) treat each channel independantly. Quaternion Convolutional Neural Networks(QCNNs) address this limitation by extending the real valued neural network framework into a four-dimensional space. In this work, we propose a Quaternion Convolutional Neural Network architecture that leverages quaternion convolution to facilitate interactions between all channels of the input and filter simultaneously using the Hamilton product. A weight initialization strategy to ensure convergence during training is adopted for the quaternion framework. The proposed model is evaluated against an equivalent real-valued CNN counterpart on the image classification task using CIFAR-10 dataset. Experimental findings indicate that the proposed QCNN achieves comparable classification accuracy while requiring approximately four times fewer trainable parameters.


