N2  - There is growing interest in quantum convolutional networks (QCNNs) due to their various possible applications and suitability for quantum computation. Although QCNN is superior in terms of performance, it requires the calls of quantum circuits for the number of windows. Parallel computation is challenging for channels with different weight filters, and there were issues with computational efficiency. In this study, we propose to improve the efficiency of the calculation algorithm by focusing on the relationship between the number of weight filters and the number of channels. We reduced the number of channels by efficiently retaining the quantum state in the next layer by observing multiple Pauli operations. We confirmed a strong correlation between the number of weight filters and the calculation time and demonstrated the importance of this method for reducing the number of weight filters. We investigated that the proposed method can significantly reduce the number of parameters and the calculation time while maintaining accuracy.


