N2  - One promising approach to accelerating AI processing on edge devices is the use of Field Programmable Gate Arrays (FPGAs). However, edge devices often face constraints such as low power consumption and restricted physical space, making AI model compression essential. To address this, we propose an approximate search method for Quantized Convolutional Neural Networks (QCNNs) using Random Forests (RF). The proposed method identifies layers that can be approximated within given accuracy requirements, while taking into account the number of operations relevant to FPGA implementation. In our experiments, the proposed method was applied to five QCNN models, and the resulting approximated QCNN models were implemented on an FPGA. We demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed method through evaluations of circuit area, execution time, dynamic power consumption, and energy consumption.


