N2  - This literature review analyses the convergence of unsupervised learning and quantum image processing for medical imaging applications. It aims to look at advancements in quantum convolutional neural networks (QC-NNs), variational quantum algorithms (VQAs), quantum-enhanced neural architectures, and hybrid quantum-classical systems with a focus on image classification and enhancement. The goal of this project is to explore possible solutions for medical image analysis, so that it can be more accurate and efficient by using unsupervised learning and quantum computing frameworks. The survey explores how quantum-assisted workflows can enhance the images from medical images, providing new avenues to diagnosis and visualization. While the NISQ era is promising, the limitations of NISQ are not permitting full quantum advantage in clinical practice at this time. To augment medical imaging with quantum-assisted unsupervised learning, this study presents research gaps and a path forward.


