N2  - The current manuscript proposes a new hybrid machine learning system, SeedNet-HDL, an intelligent hybrid of Vision Transformers (ViT), Graph Neural Networks (GNN), and Quantum-Inspired Convolutional Networks (QCNN) to analyses seed-purity without human intervention. Traditional single-algorithm designs are limited by absence of capturing of morphological and topological relationships of seed-impurity detection. The hybrid model also achieves the highest accuracy level of 98.7% by taking advantage of ViT to extract global features, GNN to model spatial-relationship features, and QCNN to represent features better. The system also includes a Federated Meta-Learning (FML) paradigm, which allows achieving continuous improvement in distributed agricultural facilities. A comprehensive data set of 25000 seed images of eight varieties of crops including experimental validation shows significant performance improvements over state-of-the-art algorithms as it achieves a precision of 98.5 and a recall of 98.9. In addition, architecture also proposes Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI) elements, enabling transparent decision-making, which will overcome the problem of the consistency of traditional deep-learned models in agriculture.


